# SHULL.OBJ - the ZSU-23-4 "Shilka" CHASSIS: tracked hull, sloped glacis,
# flat fighting deck. The turret is a SECOND model (STURR.OBJ) drawn at the
# same world point on its own yaw - the radar station's mast/dish pattern.
#
# Axes as Blender exports: -Z forward, Y up; Obj2Inc maps engine Z = -obj Z,
# so the nose points at obj -Z here and the engine sees it at +Z. The origin
# is the CENTRE OF THE DECK at ground level: y=0 is the ground the tracks
# stand on, which is what the game hands MODELDRAW as pdy.
#
# ONE OBJ UNIT = 0.2 m, and MAKE.BAT converts at -s 3, so the engine sees
# 15 units per metre: hull 99 long, 48 wide over the tracks, deck at 21.
# That is the SCALE LEVER the brief asked for - -s 2 is a tenth-scale-down
# vehicle, -s 4 a third bigger - and it was picked BY EYE at gun range, not
# by arithmetic: the F-15 is 2 units/m and a radar station about 10, but a
# 6.5 m truck at either of those is a smudge you die to without ever seeing.
# At -s 3 it is half a house long (buildings are 168..230 wide) and reads as
# a vehicle at 3000 units - which is the range you must spot it from.
#
# 18 vertices / 14 faces, against the engine's 25 / 16 per model.
#
# Real proportions, in metres: 6.6 long, 3.2 over the tracks, 1.4 to the
# deck, 0.8 to the top of the track run.
o shull

# ---- hull body: a low box, nose chamfered into the glacis ------------------
v -6.0000 4.0000 16.5000
v 6.0000 4.0000 16.5000
v 6.0000 7.0000 16.5000
v -6.0000 7.0000 16.5000
v -6.0000 7.0000 -11.0000
v 6.0000 7.0000 -11.0000
v 6.0000 4.0000 -16.5000
v -6.0000 4.0000 -16.5000
# deck seam: splits the roof into engine deck (aft) and fighting deck
v -6.0000 7.0000 2.5000
v 6.0000 7.0000 2.5000

# ---- left track run: outer face only. Its INNER top edge is the hull's own
# bottom edge (verts 1/8), which is why a track costs four vertices and not
# eight - the same trick that let the dish share the mast's cap.
v -8.0000 0.0000 14.0000
v -8.0000 0.0000 -14.0000
v -8.0000 4.0000 -16.5000
v -8.0000 4.0000 16.5000

# ---- right track run ------------------------------------------------------
v 8.0000 0.0000 14.0000
v 8.0000 0.0000 -14.0000
v 8.0000 4.0000 -16.5000
v 8.0000 4.0000 16.5000

# ---- the deck, seen from the air: two tones so the plan view has a shape
usemtl PAL17
f 9 10 6 5
usemtl PAL16
f 4 3 10 9
# ---- glacis, catching the light; the sides and stern in shade
usemtl PAL0
f 5 6 7 8
usemtl PAL16
f 1 4 5 8
f 2 3 6 7
f 1 2 3 4
# ---- the tracks: near-black, with the run rising fore and aft to the
# idler and the sprocket. The end caps are triangles closing onto the hull.
usemtl PAL3
f 11 12 13 14
usemtl PAL16
f 13 14 1 8
usemtl PAL3
f 12 13 8
f 11 14 1
f 15 16 17 18
usemtl PAL16
f 17 18 2 7
usemtl PAL3
f 16 17 7
f 15 18 2
